#!/usr/bin/env python3
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Unlicense
"""Run the PICO 4 fan from the CPU and GPU temperatures with PICO OS's policy (docs/cooling.md).

The fan hangs off the GD32 MCU that also moves the lenses and drives the
backlight. The AP reaches the MCU on /dev/ttyHS1 (115200 8N1): 6-byte
requests A0 cmd p1 p2 p3 xor; replies start with 79 and end with the XOR of the
bytes before. PICO OS's pxrfanservice sets the duty with SetFanSpeed (0x0E,
0-100 %) through gd32ipdservice:

- it samples the CPU core and GPU sensors (cpu-*-usr, gpuss-*-usr; the kernel's
  cpu*-thermal and gpu-*-thermal) every 200 ms
  and keeps each sensor's mean over its last 50 readings (10 s);
- the hottest mean picks the duty from a six-step table. On the way down a duty
  holds until the temperature falls one more step; between the two lowest
  thresholds nothing changes;
- an unchanged duty is sent again every 10 s.

PICO OS has two tables for the PICO 4 and picks one by the production batch in
the serial number ("early" and "late" here). This daemon runs the early table by
default on every headset: Valve's GPU-bound session heats the headset more than
PICO OS's own apps, and the late table's 35-50 % let it pass 90 °C. `auto` picks
by batch as PICO OS does. It adds one thing: full speed while any of those
sensors reads 95 °C or more, until the hottest mean is below 90 °C again. And one
thing for a fan that does not cool, for which PICO OS has no reaction: where PICO OS
shows its overheating notice (a hottest mean of 95.1 °C for 2 minutes), a silent MCU
or a stalled fan powers the headset off.

F1: gd32ipdservice wakes the MCU as the screen comes on (wakeUp): SetBrightness
with the configured level (sys_brt_level; 63 below 30 or without a configuration),
every 10 ms, up to 50 times, until it answers 79. This tool does the same, with 63,
when an answer is only F1, and then repeats its request once. An MCU whose update by
PICO OS failed answers F1 to everything, the wake included (docs/cooling.md).

Safety: the MCU also takes lens-motor moves, calibration writes and firmware
updates. This tool builds only the queries in QUERIES, SetFanSpeed with a duty of
0-100 and PICO OS's wake (SetBrightness with level 63); it has no way to build any
other frame.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

